## Sling — secrets and local state
#
# The whole point of the .http format is that the request file is committed and
# reviewed. That only stays safe if the secrets file never is. These entries are
# load-bearing, not housekeeping: a committed bearer token is THE known failure
# mode of .http files in the wild (Sling.md §5.1).
#
# The workspace scaffold writes these same entries into a user's own repo when it
# creates a workspace — see Sling.md §5.1. Do not remove them here on the grounds
# that this repo has no secrets yet.
*.secrets.http
.sling/secrets*
.sling/cookies*
.sling/history/
